msgid "Declares equations between terms, such as the commutativity of exponentiation in Diffie-Hellman."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:22
msgid "Declares a predicate, for clauses and for the conditions of queries."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:23
msgid "Declares a table: processes insert rows into it and look them up with get; the attacker cannot read it."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:24
msgid "Declares or executes an event: events mark points of the protocol, for correspondence queries."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:25
msgid "Asks a security property: the secrecy of a term (attacker(s)), or a correspondence between events (==>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:26
msgid "States a property that ProVerif proves first, then uses to prove the queries."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:27
msgid "States a property that ProVerif assumes without proof, to help prove the queries."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:28
msgid "Restricts the traces to those that satisfy a property."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:29
msgid "Asks for strong secrecy: the attacker cannot tell runs apart when the given names change value."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:30
msgid "Asks whether a weak secret, such as a password, resists offline guessing."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:31
msgid "A secrecy assumption: a fact that never holds. ProVerif checks it, and uses it to speed up the proof."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:32
msgid "A hint for the resolution: do not resolve on facts of this form. It changes speed and termination, not soundness."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:33
msgid "A hint for the resolution: resolve on facts of this form first."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:34
msgid "Defines a function by a term, expanded where it is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:35
msgid "Binds a variable or matches a pattern: let x = M in P. It also defines a process macro: let P(x: T) = ..."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:36
msgid "Starts the main process: the roles of the protocol, usually in parallel and replicated."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:37
msgid "Creates a fresh name that the attacker does not know: a nonce or a key."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:38
msgid "Receives a message on a channel: in(c, x: T); on a public channel it comes from the attacker. Also ends a let: let x = M in P."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:39
msgid "Sends a message on a channel: out(c, M); on a public channel the attacker gets it."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:40
msgid "A test: if M then P else Q."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:41
msgid "What runs when the test, the match or the lookup succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:42
msgid "What runs when the test, the match or the lookup fails."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:43
msgid "Inserts a row into a table: insert t(M1, ..., Mn)."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:44
msgid "Looks up a row of a table that matches a pattern: get t(=M, x) in P else Q."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:45
msgid "A condition: get ... suchthat M, or let x suchthat p(x), which picks any value that satisfies it."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:46
msgid "Starts a new phase: earlier processes stop, and the attacker keeps what it knows. Used for forward secrecy."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:47
msgid "A synchronisation barrier: processes wait for each other at sync n."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:48
msgid "A biprocess: choice[M, N] is M on the left and N on the right; ProVerif proves the two sides equivalent."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:49
msgid "A biprocess: diff[M, N] is M on the left and N on the right; ProVerif proves the two sides equivalent."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:50
msgid "The failure of a computation, such as a destructor that does not apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:51
msgid "Declares the variables of a rewrite rule, an equation, a clause or a query."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:52
msgid "Adds rules to a destructor that apply when the rules before them do not."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:53
msgid "Defines a macro of declarations, which expand instantiates."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:54
msgid "Expands a macro of declarations defined with def, with its arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:55
msgid "Sets an option of ProVerif, such as set attacker = passive."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:56
msgid "Declares channels: free names of type channel."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:57
msgid "The end of a process, as 0, in the syntax of CryptoVerif."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:58
msgid "Declares Horn clauses directly, for the attacker or for predicates."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:59
msgid "Declares a fact that always holds, to simplify the clauses."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:60
msgid "Asks whether two processes are observationally equivalent."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:61
msgid "In noninterf: the values that a secret ranges over."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:62
msgid "An injective event in a query: each occurrence matches a distinct occurrence of the events before it."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/language/PvExplain.ts:63
msgid "attacker(M): the attacker knows M. query attacker(s) asks whether s stays secret."
